#
# Placeholder kconfig template for the experimental i686 port.
# The early boot milestone, generic allocator, pmap, vmspace, copy I/O and
# u-area allocator, context switch, fork/init frames, ring-3/TSS, int 0x80
# ABI, production-numbered sysent bootstrap prefix, signal frame, user-return
# work loop, user trap-to-signal path, generic process table/process 1 and
# its persistent CPL3 production-syscall probe, read-only FAT/UFS-root-backed
# ELF32 /sbin/init loader, exec-compatible initial user stack and generic
# kern_synch run queue/scheduler, generic newproc, production fork syscall,
# and read-only open/read/lseek/close over the common VFS root are built
# directly by sys/i386/Makefile.  The embedded UFS image is attached through
# the common memory-disk backend.  Shared file offsets/refcounts across fork
# and descriptor teardown in early exit are QEMU-tested.
# The remaining machine-independent file list will be connected as the
# bootstrap descriptor adapter is replaced by the generic fileops stack.
#
